{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on 32874f97: numbers accepted. Three named numbers next.\n\nAccepted facts. Both shared cases are new in AE-1 and fail at the\nfinish forecast. The Base child at seq 1 needs 65 nodes of 64. The\nshared Grow producer at seq 0 needs 75,702,637 input work of\n67,108,864, after 45,969,870 already used. The Base root uses 58 and\n61 nodes at seq 1 and seq 2. So the witness room of AE-1 does not fit\none pass, and AE-1 cannot land with these cases red.\n\nHugh decides between a cap and a change of the work. He needs to see\nwhere the work goes. I name three numbers.\n\n1. Read only, from source and notes: what each of the two caps\n   protects. For `nodes` 64 and for `inputWork` 67,108,864, name the\n   platform limit or the measured run behind the number, with file\n   and line, or say that no source states one.\n2. Read only, from the LC-1 gate records of main: the used vector of\n   the Grow root at seq 0 under the Grow-only driver, if a record\n   prints it. Set it beside the shared vector. If no record prints\n   it, say so, and item 3 adds it.\n3. One run, granted now: your item (a). For the two refused quotes,\n   print each finish component of `archive-finish-cost.ts:97-99` as\n   a six-axis vector with its scalar inputs. Print the used vector\n   at entry to the finish. The print changes no accounting. Use a\n   never-land branch on ca1efcea and the whole unchanged owner, one\n   time, alone on the executor. The run must repeat the two refused\n   aggregate requests exactly, or it proves nothing. Stop then.\n\nYour items (b) and (c) wait. I ask for them only if Hugh or ARC-1\nnames the need.\n\nThe run takes an idle slot. It displaces no gate START and no review\nwork of C3 or SH-1. Report the three items in one act.\n\nNo source, cap, charge, assertion or deadline change in AE-1. No\nnumber of this run stands as a minimum or an acceptance.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}